"prose": [
{
"from": 122,
"to": 130,
"text": "**The gates:** - The new check, per package (gate 1). Its baseline is red because the file is absent. Its control is step 4. - The same check under `blitz-paint/font-embolden` (gate 2). This is the local witness of the macOS leg's paint   feature: canvas content takes no embolden, so the table must hold under it as the probe measured (workspace +   font-embolden, canvas png equal). - The standing readers the table sits beside, `stand_canvas_shot` and `stand_cross_os_readings`, left green (gate 3). - The pre-push gate `fast` (gate 4), which runs the workspace build of the check and `test_capability_statement.py`.   `audit` comes before the push (gate 5; security-plan · dependency-security/decision/local-audit-before-push).   `stand-repeat` takes the new `stand_` file by its prefix: three rounds, zero-failure budget (gate 6; tests S3)."
},
{
"from": 132,
"to": 135,
"text": "**What no step changes:** no boot path or binary start, so no smoke entry. No public doc comment, so no `doc` leg. No manifest or lock line, so no lock probe and no adapter re-read (a11y history n=30). No log site, span or field, no served task, kept check or committed check, and no a11y-leg file. No CI workflow line moves. There is no live leg and no headful self-verify on this project."
},
{
"from": 137,
"to": 140,
"text": "**The CI reading.** The acceptance needs CI: the table read on macOS and Windows is this chunk's point. So the operator's hygiene, push and CI entries stand (gates 7-9). The diff adds no OS `cfg` site. The OS-sensitive case is the check itself: its readings on `Test (macos)` (macOS aarch64) and `Test (windows)` (windows x86_64), whose `cargo test --all --tests` (`.github/workflows/ci.yml:344-386`) runs it beside the linux `test` leg."
}
],
